Subject: [PATCH] pandora: accept Metal's small open types on the accelerator user client

0340 was written against the pre-0336 source, where the guard read

	if (type != PANDORA_GPU_OPEN_TYPE) {

0336 rewrote that same line to

	if (type != PANDORA_GPU_OPEN_TYPE && type != 0) {

and inserted its refusal log immediately after it, so 0340's hunk no longer matched
and was dropped in silence: the k352 kernel carries 0336's "refused for %s" string
but never 0340's.  This patch is written against the post-0336 text.

Metal opens the accelerator with type 1 (log53: "24.532 IOK backboardd: open
AGXAccelerator type 1 -> 0xe00002c7"), Turnip with 0x4147; 0336 only added type 0
to the allowlist.  It is the same user client either way, so let the small numbers
through and leave 0336's log line to report whatever is still refused.

diff --git a/iokit/Kernel/arm/PandoraAdrenoGpu.cpp b/iokit/Kernel/arm/PandoraAdrenoGpu.cpp
--- a/iokit/Kernel/arm/PandoraAdrenoGpu.cpp
+++ b/iokit/Kernel/arm/PandoraAdrenoGpu.cpp
@@ -548,6 +548,10 @@
 pandora_gpu_new_client(IOService *owner, task_t owningTask, void *securityID, UInt32 type, IOUserClient **handler)
 {
-	if (type != PANDORA_GPU_OPEN_TYPE && type != 0) {
+	/*
+	 * 0342: Metal asks for type 1, Turnip for 0x4147. Same client, so accept the
+	 * small numbers as well; 0336's log line below still reports anything else.
+	 */
+	if (type != PANDORA_GPU_OPEN_TYPE && type > 8) {
 		char who[32];
 		proc_selfname(who, sizeof(who));
 		IOLog("PANDORA GPU ES: open type 0x%x refused for %s\n", type, who);
